From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:48:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] tools: asahi: give the T6030 graph harness the two names the
 extracted report probe now uses

The report probe tells the AGX vote that a T6001 report came back
(apple_pmp_agx_activity_resume) and compares rep->offsets with the T6001
table. The harness extracts the probe verbatim and compiles it standalone, so
production.h failed with an undeclared apple_pmp_offsets_t600x and an
implicit declaration of apple_pmp_agx_activity_resume.

An empty T6001 table that never matches and an empty resume function are
enough: the harness models the T6030 graph. All 21 graph cases pass, and the
supplier harness passes (ASan needs ASLR off on this host: setarch -R).

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit e8ddbd9fff0252ef8aeb95a3463cf1b8b1ce24c1)
---
 tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c b/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c
index d7d079a967..38d10db885 100644
--- a/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c
+++ b/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c
@@ -584,6 +584,10 @@ static const struct apple_pmp_start_ops apple_pmp_start_hw_ops = { hw_check,
 								   hw_bound };
 static const struct apple_pmp_start_timing apple_pmp_start_timing = { 2, 0, 2,
 								      2 };
+/* The extracted probe compares rep->offsets with the T6001 table and tells the AGX vote that a report came back. This harness has neither: the table is empty and
+ * never matches, and the call does nothing. */
+static const struct apple_pmp_report_offsets apple_pmp_offsets_t600x;
+static void apple_pmp_agx_activity_resume(void) {}
 #include "production.h"
 static const struct apple_pmp_report_offsets *
 of_device_get_match_data(struct device *d)
